When we look at the sampling distribution of \(\hat\Delta_0\), we see no bias at all. And it’s not because our covariate distributions are close to the same in the two groups. They’re not. Something else is going on. It’s about the relationship between our model and these covariate distributions. If you change the model to the horizontal lines model, you’ll get bias.10
